  "emailBody": "\n        <html>\n\n        <body\n            style=\"\n                font-family:Segoe UI, Arial, sans-serif;\n                margin:20px;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    background:#d42e12;\n                    color:white;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                \"\n            >\n\n\n               <h1 style=\"margin:0;\">\n                    Fuel Market Intelligence Afternoon Report\n                </h1>\n\n                <p style=\"margin:5px 0 0 0;\">\n                    20 August 2026\n                </p>\n\n            </div>\n\n            <p\n                style=\"\n                    font-size:16px;\n                    margin-top:20px;\n                    margin-bottom:20px;\n                \"\n            >\n                Good afternoon Sir,\n                <br><br>\n                \n                Here is today's fuel market intelligence report highlighting\n                the latest PMS and AGO depot prices together with key industry\n                developments and market news.\n            </p>\n\n            <br>\n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            PMS Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average PMS Prices: ₦1,201.25/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>LIQUID BULK</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MRS TINCAN</td>\n                <td>₦1,167.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NEPAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,168.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,195.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX PH</td>\n                <td>₦1,220.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,215.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            AGO Prices\n        </h2>\n\n        <div\n            style=\"\n                background:#fad5a1;\n                padding:12px;\n                border-left:5px solid #f28e05;\n                margin-bottom:10px;\n                font-size:16px;\n                font-weight:bold;\n            \"\n        >\n            Average AGO Prices: ₦1,688.12/L\n        </div>\n\n        <table\n            width=\"100%\"\n            cellspacing=\"0\"\n            cellpadding=\"10\"\n            style=\"\n                border-collapse:collapse;\n                border:1px solid #ddd;\n            \"\n        >\n\n            <tr style=\"background:#d42e12;color:white;\">\n                <th align=\"left\">Depot</th>\n                <th align=\"left\">Price</th>\n            </tr>\n\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>PRUDENT OGHARA</td>\n                <td>₦1,695.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>NIPCO WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,695.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,690.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,575.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>BULK STRATEGIC</td>\n                <td>₦1,705.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,685.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,800.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,660.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Atiku Pledges to Restore Fuel Subsidy if Elected in 2027\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Former Vice President Atiku Abubakar has pledged to reinstate Nigeria’s fuel subsidy if he wins the presidency in the 2027 general election. Atiku, who is the presidential candidate of the African Democratic Congress (ADC), said he initially did not oppose the decision to remove the subsidy. The decision led to a sharp increase in petrol prices and contributed to higher transportation costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/atiku-pledges-to-restore-fuel-subsidy-if-elected-in-2027\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Regulatory Uncertainty Could Drive Investors Away From Nigeria’s Oil Sector – Osifo\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    PENGASSAN President, Comrade Festus Osifo, called for a predictable, transparent and efficient regulatory system. He said the Petroleum Industry Act, PIA, 2021, was a major milestone in the country’s long-running effort to reform the sector.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/regulatory-uncertainty-could-drive-investors-away-from-nigerias-oil-sector-osifo\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Subsidy, ₦200/Litre Petrol Price Would Have Crushed Dangote Refinery — FG\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has said that the Dangote Petroleum Refinery could not have operated commercially under Nigeria’s former petrol subsidy regime. The Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of the Economy, Taiwo Oyedele, stated this in Abuja. He said the removal of the petrol subsidy, alongside the unification of the foreign exchange market, came with significant costs.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/subsidy-200litre-petrol-price-would-have-crushed-dangote-refinery-fg\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG: No 'Subsidy Savings' Line Exists as ₦15.8trn Already Outspent — Oyedele\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's Federal Government has clarified that the ₦15.8 trillion in resources mobilised from subsidy removal and foreign exchange reforms did not translate into a pool of unspent cash. Finance Minister and Coordinating Minister of the Economy, Taiwo Oyedele, disclosed this while presenting the government's Reform Scorecard.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-no-subsidy-savings-line-exists-as-158trn-already-outspent-oyedele\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    EFCC Recovers ₦4.5bn Diesel From Ibafon Depot as Prudent Energy Alleges Diversion\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Economic and Financial Crimes Commission (EFCC) has recovered 2.3 million litres of Automotive Gas Oil (AGO), commonly known as diesel, from Ibafon Oil and Gas in Lagos. The recovery was carried out on Monday, August 17, 2026, by the EFCC’s Lagos Zonal Directorate 1 after a petition by Prudent Energy and Services Limited. The commission said the outstanding stock was initially recorded at 2,574,031 litres following periodic withdrawals.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/efcc-recovers-45bn-diesel-from-ibafon-depot-as-prudent-energy-alleges-diversion\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
